      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright (c) 2008 Elsevier Ireland Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A 61-year-old man was referred at our hospital for a cardiac evaluation after an episode of oppressive chest pain at rest. He was discharged with a MRI diagnosis of non-compaction cardiomyopathy presented with typical angina, left ventricle dysfunction and ischemic EKG findings without atherosclerotic narrowing and also with a type B aortic dissection, documented also by computed tomography."
